9. SMART LISTENING ARCHITECTURE
==================================================

The bot must NOT continuously consume and process every group message.

Implement intent-based listening.

Default state:

- minimal passive event handling
- no unnecessary message-content processing
- no broad message listener performing expensive work

When the user activates listening for a target group:

.listen 5m

or similar configuration,

the bot temporarily enables command/event handling only for the relevant target/group context.

Rules:

- timer controlled
- auto-expire
- group-specific
- command-specific when possible
- no global listener
- no unnecessary message storage
- no unnecessary processing
- no regression to normal sending functionality

If another relevant command is opened in another target group, switch the active listener context cleanly.

Prefer event routing and lightweight filters over processing every message.

Do not confuse “not listening” with “bot being offline”.

The bot must still be capable of sending scheduled/authorized outbound operations.

